My only complaint about this zone is:<P>There is really only one good camp for our group and that is the ever popular CourtYard ( CY ).  <P>The other camps have more sentry's then guardians and aren't as dense in mobs...meaning we would get bored real fast pulling 5 mobs from the Kitchen area or 4 from the Dinning Room.  Yeah, you might be able to hold both areas, but every single time I've  been there, someone moves in on the one room you're not sitting next too.<P>Looking at the map, you would think that the area past the CY is good, but I conned some of them and they were 50th and half of them saw thru inviso.   <IMG SRC="frown.gif" border="0"><P>So, basicaly I'd say we try to get them stupid sticks for the Bracer quest we started, then next time...if CY camped and no one else can think of something better to kill in SS, we head elsewhere for excitement.<P>Tower of Frozen Shadow for a 3rd,4th and 5th floor attempt.<P>GD to kill some of Medec's long lost cousins ( if we wanna go giant faction )<P>Kael to kill some giants to repair the CoV faction hits.  ( if we wanna go back to Dragon )<P>EW to maybe try for some Ry'gorr armor and exp.<P>Kaesora should still have some good exp and drops a little deeper in.<P>Droga same as Kaesora.<P>The Hole entrance<P>Kedge Keep...but not sure where since we tried that and due to levels decided to come back later when we could take a named room or two.<P>Also...Brinne and Brod could log and try and get some extra exp there by joining a pickup group or two...or talking Lownar into coming back and grouping with him.  Medec is still bound there, so if trouble hit and a rezz was need, I can gate him back.  Would be good for Lownar cause he wouldn't need to pull once he got the spawn broken and good for Brod since it would let him see how the zone worked for when we hit it.<P>--------------------<P>Verser - Bard of the 51st Song
</FONT>
